From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: jz4740: trace the SDIO clock only for the LPM-workaround host

Bring-up aid for the ATBM6031 SDIO host on 7.1.  jz4740_mmc_set_ios()
reaches jz4740_mmc_set_clock_rate() on every bus-clock programming, and
the MMC core does that repeatedly during card detection, so an
unconditional print floods the boot log - and mostly traces the wrong
host: the MSC0 card slot fires it more often than the MSC1 SDIO host.

Gate the print on host->sdio_clk so only the controller that opted into
the ingenic,sdio_clk workaround is traced, and report the requested rate,
the achieved rate, the divider and the bus width rather than the achieved
rate alone.

Temporary: drop this patch once the SDIO host enumerates.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
@@ -922,6 +922,14 @@ static int jz4740_mmc_set_clock_rate(struct jz4740_mmc_host *host, int rate)
 				   host->base + JZ_REG_MMC_LPM);
 	}
 
+	/* SDIO bring-up aid: trace only the host that opts into the LPM
+	 * workaround, not every MMC controller. */
+	if (host->sdio_clk)
+		dev_info(&host->pdev->dev,
+			 "%s: req=%d real=%d div=%d width=%d sdio_clk=%d\n",
+			 mmc_hostname(host->mmc), rate, real_rate, div,
+			 host->mmc->ios.bus_width, host->sdio_clk);
+
 	return real_rate;
 }
 
